// This workspace ties arnon's three modules together for local development and
// CI. It is committed on purpose: until the root module's first tag exists,
// the submodules' `require github.com/casara/arnon v0.0.0` cannot resolve from
// the module proxy, so without the workspace the repository does not build.
//
// Consumers never see this file - `go.work` is ignored outside the workspace
// root, so it has no effect on anyone who runs `go get github.com/casara/arnon`.
//
// See docs/architecture/adr-0001-module-layout.md for the release ordering:
// tag the root module first, then bump the submodules' require, then tag them.
go 1.26

use (
	.
	./examples
	./observability/otel
)
